From 9720823c814691ca1455cbef65d13c629fac2a60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JuggyMcNutty <11588877+JuggyMcNutty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 09:19:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Actor iterators: the slots of a class from an index, not a
 scan

FORK ONLY. This project ships a NO-AI Code Rule asking that LLM-written
changes stay in a fork and are never PR'd upstream. These were written with
Claude. Do not submit them.

The actor iterators found the actors of a class by testing every actor in
the level: on Liberty Island ~2,500, a cache miss each on the handheld's
Cortex-A53. Every NPC's ScriptedPawn.CheckEnemyPresence steps through the
pawns with CycleActors each tick, and a CPU sample of the device's game
tick put CycleActorsIterator::Next at 17.6% of it, ~16 ms a frame; the name
tests of AllActors, RadiusActors and VisibleActors (UObject::IsA) came
next.

- The level keeps, per class asked for, the slots of Actors holding one:
  ULevelBase::ActorsByClass for CycleActors, which tests the class by
  pointer, and ActorsByClassName for the others, which test it by name.
  Each is rebuilt when ActorsVersion has moved: Load, the GameInfo, Spawn,
  Destroy and the compaction bump it. Destroyed actors stay in an index
  and are skipped where they were skipped.
- CycleActors binary-searches the next slot after the current one, going
  round, and counts the slots the scan would have passed, so the lap ends
  where the scan's did. Unusual states (no class, an empty level, a start
  past the end) still scan.
- AllActors steps through the slots from its position; RadiusActors and
  VisibleActors build their lists from them.
- ULevel::Tick rebuilt the actor list every frame to drop nulled slots,
  rewriting every actor's Index. It now does so only after a Destroy has
  nulled one (and once after loading, as before); without holes the result
  was the same list.

Temporary checks ran the scans beside the indexes from the same state on
Liberty Island: 2.9 million CycleActors steps (same actor, slot and end of
lap), 36,366 AllActors steps, and 1,817 RadiusActors and VisibleActors
lists built beside AllActors calls, all the same. The CycleActors index was
rebuilt 68 times in 8,571 frames.
